WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.202
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian and actor you know

00:00:03.202 --> 00:00:04.503
from
"The King of Staten Island."

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:07.307
His comedy special "Ricky Velez:
Here's Everything"

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.944
premieres October 23rd on HBO
as well as streaming on HBO Max.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.078
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:13.379
-By the way,
I'm Irish and Puerto Rican.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.515
That's my mix.
That's what it is.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:18.551
[ Cheers ]
No, no, no, no.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.353
No, those people
should not hang out.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:24.824
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:27.160
Irish and Puerto Rican.
I'm just happy I'm not gay

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.261
because that's way too many
parades to go to.

00:00:29.261 --> 00:00:32.498
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:34.967
"Yo, where's Ricky at?"
"He got another parade, dawg.

00:00:34.967 --> 00:00:38.004
He can't chill.
Sundays aren't good for him.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.839
Don't hit him up on Sundays.
He parades a lot.

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:44.410
If you need him, he's on Fifth.
You go if you need him."

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:47.180
-Please welcome to the show
Ricky Velez, everybody!

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.115
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:56.956 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:04.831 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.999
Welcome to the show!
I'm so happy to have you.

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:09.301
-You have an audience.
-We have an audience.

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:11.971
And they're very happy.
-You have an audience.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.909
-I'm especially happy
to have a stand-up out here

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.611
because I feel like, of everyone
who was robbed of an audience,

00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:22.782
you know, I think live musicians
and stand-up comedians,

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.584
it was just, like,
the hardest thing to do.

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.852
You had a special ready to go.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.821
COVID hit,
and you basically had to wait,

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:30.790
I mean, I guess about
a year and a half.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.158
-I got canceled by God.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:33.560
[ Laughter ]
-You got canceled by God.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.161
That's the real cancellation,
yeah.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.631
-God was like, "Not today."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.333
-When you first started
doing shows again,

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.067
because I know a lot of
comedians tried to figure out

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.470
weird ways to do shows,
did you any strange ones?

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.771
-Yeah, I did a few.

00:01:45.771 --> 00:01:48.707
I had to stand in front of cars
and yell at them.

00:01:48.707 --> 00:01:50.443
-You did some of
those car shows?

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.311
-They just beep,
and that means they're happy.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.847
[ Laughter ]
It's usually the opposite.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:56.882
-Yeah, it must be hard to rewire
the brain.

00:01:56.882 --> 00:01:59.185
-They made me do a show
on a farm.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.720
-What?

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.323
-You don't know how bad you're
doing until you hear a moo.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.490
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.358
It was terrible.

00:02:06.358 --> 00:02:07.726
-So the moo is not like a beep?

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.095
The moo is not
"you're doing well"?

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.998
-Well, it's also weird when
your green room is a barn.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.165
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.500
You just start feeling like --

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.602
You're like,
"This is not Hollywood anymore."

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:18.504
[ Laughter ]
"This is strange."

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:23.709
-It must be nice to finally have
shot it and have it,

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.644
you know,
available for people to see.

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:27.646
-I guess.
-Alright.

00:02:27.646 --> 00:02:30.015
[ Laughter ]
We appreciate your honesty.

00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:32.618
[ Laughter ]
One thing we have in common,

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:34.753
I think, you know,
when we do stand-up,

00:02:34.753 --> 00:02:35.988
we like to talk
about our family.

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:39.559
You got a 3-year-old?
-Yeah.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.628
-Was it nice to be able to go
out and talk about him?

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:44.096
-I mean, I needed to get away
from him.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:45.698
-Yeah. It's a nice reason, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.399
-We just did a full year
together.

00:02:47.399 --> 00:02:49.001
I'm out. I'm done.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.638
I'm getting back on the road.
Miami is nice, you know?

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.039
[ Laughter ]
-"I'm getting out on the road,

00:02:54.039 --> 00:02:56.509
and I'm going to talk about you,
kid."

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.110
Is he pretty good
at giving you material?

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.381
Do you feel like --
You know, again, as a stand-up,

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:02.949
I think that's the reason
to have kids.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.685
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.753
-No, I think I get more
from my wife.

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.221
-Yeah. How is she with it?

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:12.658
Is she okay with you taking --
-Time to time.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:17.430
But, like, she knows she beats
me, like, mind-wise.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.599
Like, she's very educated.
-Yep.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.601
-And I went to a school
with a commercial.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.204
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.438
-Yeah.

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:28.541
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.610
-That's not a good school.
-Yeah.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:32.311
[ Applause ]

00:03:32.311 --> 00:03:34.413
I feel like that's the break.
It's either, like,

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:37.617
was there a seal with
Latin words or a commercial?

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:38.651
-No, it was the one with the guy

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:41.020
standing in front of
the blue Subaru.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.889
He was like, "Life was bad,
but now I got a Subaru."

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.792
And I was like,
"I need a Subaru."

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.093
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.093 --> 00:03:50.964
-Another thing we have in
common, I'm married to a lawyer,

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.765
so in arguments, I tend to lose.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.333
I would imagine, based on what
you're saying here,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:55.834
you don't do particularly well
when you argue.

00:03:55.834 --> 00:03:57.704
-No. Yeah.

00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:00.840
She just goes, "You went to
a college with a commercial."

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.742
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:06.579
-You have very good producers
on this special -- Judd Apatow

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.748
and your friend Pete Davidson.
-People like those guys.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.950
-Yeah, they like those guys.
Good guys.

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:14.821
You met --
I guess you guys were kids

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.422
when you met doing stand-up,
you and Pete?

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:20.426
-Yeah, me and Pete --
I was 21, he was 16.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.128
He was like,
"Will you get me a beer?"

00:04:22.128 --> 00:04:23.896
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.698
I was like, "Alright, kid."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.698 --> 00:04:29.001
And, yeah, we became friends,
and we just kicked it.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.437
And it was fun.
We lived together.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:34.040
-What was it like when Ricky
and Pete were living together?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.774
-Our parents did not like it.

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:37.009
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:39.878
-We only made it eight months.
-What happened?

00:04:39.878 --> 00:04:42.448
-Just everything turned into
an ashtray.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.249
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:46.719
I woke up once.
He was using my belly button.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.886
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.886 --> 00:04:49.756
I was like, "Come on, man,
use your own."

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.490
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.159
-Does he have an outie? I feel
bad for people with outie.

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.094
-That's what the problem is.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.696
-You got an outie,
all of a sudden the ashes

00:04:56.696 --> 00:05:00.199
are all over your whole belly,
yeah.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.800
I want to talk about,
while we're talking about

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.202
belly buttons,
I have a photographic --

00:05:04.202 --> 00:05:05.438
So, you made a choice.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.139
This was not something
you were forced to do.

00:05:07.139 --> 00:05:08.241
-I made a choice on this one.

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:10.376
-I want to make it clear
this wasn't HBO.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.078
-No, Judd did not make me
do this.

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:15.781
-Okay. So, this is -- Do you
want to talk real quick about

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.583
what you decided to do for
the poster of your special?

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:20.819
-So, Mark Seliger,
amazing photographer.

00:05:20.819 --> 00:05:23.789
The guy's a legend.
He shot Obama. He's incredible.

00:05:23.789 --> 00:05:25.090
And Judd called me
and he's like,

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.926
"He's going to shoot you
for the special."

00:05:27.926 --> 00:05:30.329
And I started going
through his book,

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:33.365
and I saw that he shot
Kim Kardashian nude.

00:05:33.365 --> 00:05:36.835
So I was like, "He's going to
shoot Ricky Velez nude."

00:05:36.835 --> 00:05:38.805
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.840
And he did.
-He shot me nude, yeah.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:46.845
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:51.617
I got to do this
in front of HBO execs.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.152
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.853
Do you think at any point
the photographer was like,

00:05:54.853 --> 00:05:56.722
"Aw, man, I shot Obama"?

00:05:56.722 --> 00:05:58.424
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.959
-At one point he turned to me,
he goes, "I'm nervous."

00:06:00.959 --> 00:06:05.064
[ Laughter ]
I was like, "Shut up."

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.832
-Did you find --

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.635
First of all, did you work out
before you took the shot?

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.904
-I was on one. Yeah, no, yeah.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.305
-Alright. That's good.
-All of that.

00:06:13.305 --> 00:06:16.275
-And then did you become
comfortable the longer you were

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:18.177
fully naked in front of
a room full of people?

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:20.646
-Well, it was weird because,
like, I had to keep myself

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:23.849
covered for it, and then,
like, we had stuff pop out.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:25.117
And Mark was such a gentleman.

00:06:25.117 --> 00:06:26.719
He'd just be like,
"Ricky, move your hand

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:27.887
a little bit more to the right."

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:30.656
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.959
"You're ruining a great day."

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:36.095
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.696
He's like, "You sure
you don't want to take

00:06:37.696 --> 00:06:38.898
any options with clothes on?"

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.833
I was like, "Nope!"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.668
I was like,
"You definitely didn't say that

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:44.837
to Kim Kardashian."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.837 --> 00:06:48.640
-"Let's get a coat on Kim."

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.978
Your son was born --
I mean, you know, I, obviously,

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:54.480
have talked about the way my
kids were born over the years.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.482
How was yours?
-Not in a lobby.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:59.551
-No, yeah. Well-planned.
-Yeah.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:02.155
No, but he was born on 9/11.
-Okay.

00:07:02.155 --> 00:07:04.022
-Yeah, he was born on 9/11.

00:07:04.022 --> 00:07:06.191
He's Irish, Puerto Rican,
and Jewish.

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:09.294
So he's the most New York thing
you can get.

00:07:09.294 --> 00:07:11.096
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:13.833
-Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:16.135
-Kid loves a bagel.
-He loves a bagel.

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.736
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:20.705
Did you participate
in the birth?

00:07:20.705 --> 00:07:22.775
No? Okay. You were there?

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:24.309
-I was behind the sheet.
-Yeah, okay.

00:07:24.309 --> 00:07:26.345
-I didn't want to see it.

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:28.647
I'm not good with blood.
I didn't want to go down.

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:29.949
And my wife turned to me
right before

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:31.417
she was going to have the kid,
she goes,

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:33.585
"If you're going to make this
about you, you need to leave."

00:07:33.585 --> 00:07:36.922
[ Laughter ]
That's true.

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:40.459
And then through the curtain,

00:07:40.459 --> 00:07:42.728
the doctor's like, "You want to
cut the umbilical cord?"

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.764
And I didn't know that word,
like --

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:47.966
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.966 --> 00:07:50.235
I went to a college with
a commercial, right?

00:07:50.235 --> 00:07:53.205
So I was like, "No, I don't want
to cut the ability cord."

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:54.773
And the doctor --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.773 --> 00:07:56.275
The doctor was like,
"Umbilical cord."

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.676
And I was like, "Ability cord."

00:07:57.676 --> 00:08:00.312
He's like, "Sir, I'm pretty sure
you're saying ability cord."

00:08:00.312 --> 00:08:02.648
I was like,
"I'm 100% saying ability cord."

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:03.950
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.717
And he goes, "Why would you ever
call it that?"

00:08:05.717 --> 00:08:07.954
And I was like, "Well, it gives
the baby abilities, correct?"

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:09.888
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.888 --> 00:08:11.624
And he said,
"That's not as dumb as I thought

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:14.694
it was going to be."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:14.694 --> 00:08:16.228
"Good luck."

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:18.029
-They're going to put you
in front of the Subaru

00:08:18.029 --> 00:08:19.064
on the new commercial.

00:08:19.064 --> 00:08:20.599
Hey, man, congrats
on the special.

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:22.134
-Thank you so much
for having me.

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.203
-Really appreciate
having you out here tonight.

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:25.671
Such a delight.
-Thank you so much.

00:08:25.671 --> 00:08:29.975
-"Ricky Velez: Here's
Everything" premieres on HBO

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:32.044
and is streaming on HBO Max
on October 23rd.

